[15.338,"o","\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[15.346,"o","# Mission: fix hello world greeting (parallix-adhoc-0001)\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\nMake `./hello.sh` print the exact string `Hello, World!` so that `./scripts/verify-local.sh` passes. The root cause is a typo in the `printf` format string in `hello.sh`, which currently emits `Helo, Wrld!` instead of `Hello, World!`.\r\n\r\n## Why Now\r\nThe repository's only verification gate, `./scripts/verify-local.sh`, fails on the current tree because `hello.sh` outputs `Helo, Wrld!`. This is a regression-style break: the expected output is fixed by the test, and the source simply does not produce it. Fixing it restores the one green path the repo has and validates the draft→execute→integrate workflow on a minimal tree.\r\n\r\n## Refinement Signals\r\n- Predicted NEL bucket: Small (0–80)\r\n- Confidence: High\r\n- Selection note: activate as-is\r\n- Main drivers: single-line source typo, one failing gate, no dependencies, no new files.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n- Edit `hello.sh` so its `printf` emits `Hello, World!\\n`.\r\n- Run `./scripts/verify-local.sh` and confirm it exits 0.\r\n- Preserve the script's shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env bash`) and the `# Hello world` comment header.\r\n"]
[19.346,"o","\r\n## Out of Scope\r\n- Adding new files, tests, or dependencies.\r\n- Changing the verification command in `scripts/verify-local.sh` or `workflow.config.json`.\r\n- Refactoring the script into a language other than bash.\r\n- Adding argument parsing, localization, or any greeting beyond the single hardcoded string.\r\n- Any graphify index changes (no source files other than `hello.sh` are touched).\r\n\r\n## Success Criteria\r\n> **Falsifiability rule (ADR 0039 Part 2):** Each criterion must be falsifiable.\r\n\r\n- `./hello.sh` outputs exactly `Hello, World!` followed by a trailing newline and nothing else.\r\n- `./scripts/verify-local.sh` exits with status 0 (currently fails: `test \"$(./hello.sh)\" = \"Hello, World!\"`).\r\n- `hello.sh` remains executable (mode `0755`) and retains its `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang.\r\n- No other files in the repo are modified.\r\n\r\n## Risks and Assumptions\r\n- Assumption: the canonical expected output is the literal `Hello, World!`, as encoded in `scripts/verify-local.sh`. If that test is edited, the contract target changes — do not edit that test.\r\n- Risk: introducing a trailing space, missing newline, or wrong casing via the `printf` format string will silently fail the equality test.\r\n- Assumption: execution environment has `bash` and `printf` available (standard on the target platform).\r\n\r\n## Checkpoints\r\n- CP 1: Author a failing reproduction of the greeting bug. Run `./hello.sh` and confirm output is `Helo, Wrld!` (not `Hello, World!`) at the mission's parent commit — this is the red state.\r\n- CP 2: Fix the `printf` format string in `hello.sh` to emit `Hello, World!`.\r\n- CP 3: Run `./scripts/verify-local.sh` and confirm it exits 0 (green state); record evidence in the Goal Check table.\r\n\r\n### Checkpoint Documentation Requirements\r\nEvery checkpoint document (CP-N.md) MUST include:\r\n- A summary of work done\r\n- A `## Goal Check` section\r\n- A 3-column pipe-delimited markdown table with columns: Criterion | Evidence | Status\r\n- At least one evidence row per criterion using durable, verifiable references. Parallix already accepts:\r\n  1. **Recognized repo commands or paths** — e.g., `` `./scripts/verify-local.sh` ``, `` `./hello.sh` ``\r\n  2. **Test names** — must match a test name in the repo (if any exist)\r\n  3. **Test file paths** — e.g., `scripts/verify-local.sh` (must be an existing file)\r\n  4. **ADR references** — e.g., `ADR 0039` (must correspond to an existing file under `docs/adr/`)\r\n  5. **File:line references** — accepted when needed, but line numbers eventually rot; prefer the forms above\r\n- Raw `stat`/`ls` output or generic prose may appear as supplemental context, but pair them with one of the accepted references above. Concretely: raw shell output such as `echo \"$(./hello.sh)\"` or `ls -l hello.sh` is NOT sufficient on its own — pair it with a recognized repo command/path (e.g. `` `./scripts/verify-local.sh` ``) or the test file path `scripts/verify-local.sh`.\r\n- A non-generic `Next action:` line at the bottom\r\n\r\nExample Goal Check table:\r\n\r\n"]
[23.346,"o","| Criterion | Evidence | Status |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `./hello.sh` prints `Hello, World!` | `./hello.sh` → `Hello, World!` | PASS |\r\n| Verification gate passes | `./scripts/verify-local.sh` exits 0 | PASS |\r\n| Script remains executable with shebang | `head -1 hello.sh` → `#!/usr/bin/env bash`; `ls -l hello.sh` | PASS |\r\n\r\n## Gates\r\n- [ ] ./scripts/verify-local.sh\r\n\r\n## Restricted Areas\r\n- Do not modify `scripts/verify-local.sh`, `workflow.config.json`, or any file under `config/`.\r\n- Do not create, rename, or delete files.\r\n- Do not run any test runner or gate other than `./scripts/verify-local.sh`.\r\n- Do not start a review, execute, or integrate phase; do not transition the backlog task.\r\n\r\n## Stop Rules\r\n- Stop after the draft is verified clean with `./scripts/verify-local.sh` and the Goal Check evidence is recorded.\r\n- Do not implement the fix; this draft phase produces the mission contract only.\r\n- Do not edit the backlog task `assignee` field.\r\n- Stop if `scripts/verify-local.sh` itself is found to define a different expected output — re-read the gate before proceeding.\r\n"]
